# Build context of apps/mock-server/Dockerfile (the only image; `docker build` / `flyctl deploy`
# from the repository root). An allowlist: everything is excluded except what the image copies,
# which keeps out node_modules (pnpm junctions on Windows), .git, agent worktrees, .local, .env
# files and build or test output, and keeps the upload to Fly's builder small.
# Exceptions name literal paths, no wildcards: the tar walker flyctl uses (moby go-archive) skips
# an excluded directory unless an exception starts with its literal path.
*

!package.json
!pnpm-lock.yaml
!pnpm-workspace.yaml

# Every workspace manifest, so the workspace matches the lockfile's importers.
!apps/mock-server/package.json
!apps/web/package.json
!packages/protocol/package.json

# Docker and flyctl add the Dockerfile back on their own; Fly's docs ask to keep it in the context.
!apps/mock-server/Dockerfile

# Runtime sources: the server and the workspace packages it imports.
!apps/mock-server/src
!packages/protocol/src

# Tests and benchmarks never run in the image.
**/*.test.ts
**/*.bench.ts
